  "prefLabel": "Cul-H 102.40 Skeletal analyst",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Cul-H 102.40 “Skeletal analyst” means “skeletal analyst” pursuant to RSA 227-C:1, VIII-a, that is, the member of the professional staff or another professional person designated by the director of the division of historical resources with the approval of the commissioner to analyze suspected human skeletal remains.\n\nSource. #10217, eff 10-30-12, EXPIRED: 7-1-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/cul-h100.html"
